    sol: "# Trigger: a scheduled build (weekly, for OS security patches) OR a CI trigger on a change\n# to the provisioning scripts/Ansible playbook baked into the image.\n\n# Pipeline: Packer builds a new AMI -> runs a smoke test against a temporary instance from\n# that AMI -> if healthy, tags the new AMI as 'latest-approved'.\n\n# Rollout to running instances: golden images do NOT auto-update running instances -- a new\n# AMI only affects instances launched AFTER it's built. Getting existing instances onto it\n# requires a Terraform apply that updates the Auto Scaling Group's launch template to\n# reference the new AMI ID, combined with an instance refresh (AWS's native rolling-\n# replacement mechanism for an ASG) so old instances are drained and replaced with new ones.",
